DOC|dev_process|v1|updated=2026-03-13
META|purpose=how Akien and Claude Code work together; conventions Igor should know
META|audience=Igor reading this to understand the development context he exists in

CONTEXT|
  primary_dev_tool=Claude Code (CC); never aider/Gemini/other LLMs (they make messes)
  igor_uses=OpenRouter; CC uses Anthropic direct — keep separate to control token costs
  igor_self_edits=auto-commit+push via self_edit.py; CC edits do NOT auto-commit
  commit_policy=never --no-verify; never force-push main; commit at logical checkpoints only

WORKFLOW|
  session_start=CC reads CLAUDE.md + design_docs_for_igor/ DSBs; no recap needed
  plan_first=discuss plan with Akien before doing the work; no unilateral big changes
  plan_approval="i like your plan, go" is a real step; see the whole move before making it
  tickets=each piece of work has a GitHub issue; each session has a sprint discussion
  save_plans=GitHub discussions for recoverability across sessions
  gap_analysis=update design_docs_for_igor/gap_analysis.dsb as gaps close or new ones found
  master_plan=https://github.com/akienm/TheIgors/discussions/62 — update end of each session

CORRECTION_DISCIPLINE|
  correct_immediately=every mistake named precisely in the moment; don't let things slide
  feedback_persists=CC stores corrections in ~/.claude/projects/.../memory/; applies next session
  why=uncorrected mistake becomes pattern; correction compounds forward

CODE_QUALITY|
  read_before_edit=always read a file before modifying; never overwrite blindly
  check_inertia=check inertia_registry.dsb before editing; HIGH needs Akien review
  check_design_docs=read relevant design docs before architectural changes
  minimal_changes=don't add features, refactor, docstrings, comments beyond what was asked
  no_silent_exceptions=every except block must log or re-raise; see standards.dsb RULE_NO_SILENT_EXCEPTIONS
  no_mocks=tests against real systems; fixture data in DB; rollback if writes needed

SELF_EDIT_CONVENTIONS|
  preferred=patch_source_file (line-range + syntax check)
  after_patch=reload_module() if module is hot-reloadable; else restart
  blocked=brainstem/ without Akien review
  auto=git commit+push after success
  igor_edits_auto_commit=yes; CC edits do NOT

INERTIA_LEVELS|see inertia_registry.dsb
  HIGH=discuss with Akien; never edit casually; strong justification required
  MEDIUM=discuss before editing
  LOW=freely improvable; hot-reloadable where stateless

TESTING_PHILOSOPHY|
  no_mocks=mocked tests verify the mock not the behavior
  real_systems=tests against real SQLite, real OR calls (with fixture data)
  design_for_testability=injectable seams, fixture DB snapshots, rollback support
  igor_participates=Igor knows he's in test context (TWM flag); test run = curriculum
  smoke_tests=thin layer of structural tests; runs in <10s before restart
  future=self-programming epic (#206) — Igor generates + runs his own tests

ARCHITECTURAL_PRINCIPLES|see architecture_root.dsb CORE_PRINCIPLES (canonical location 2026-04-14)
